From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] quartz: Implement the RGB Color Space Converter filter.

The Witch's Love Diary explicitly instantiates CLSID_Colour while building
its WMV playback graph. The class is missing, so CoCreateInstance fails
with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG and the application skips the opening movie.
The reporter's log records both the missing class and the subsequent
"Video Mpeg : CoCreateInstance CLSID_Colour" / "Video : Load" failures.

Implement a normal DirectShow RGB transform in quartz, using memory DIBs
for color conversion. Preserve sample timestamps, flags, seeking and
streaming events, and validate format blocks, palette/mask sizes, image
dimensions and sample lengths. Handle RGB8/555/565/24/32, DWORD-aligned rows,
and top-down and bottom-up DIBs. This neither decodes compressed video
nor changes the shared winedmo decoder or Media Foundation paths.

Register the class and its filter pins with the documented MERIT_UNLIKELY,
so directly connected decoder/renderer graphs retain priority. Add tests
for class activation, pin interfaces, rejected media types, RGB conversion
with odd widths and all row orientations, timing, flushing and EOF.
No title-specific override or native quartz installation is required.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/755
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/directshow/color-space-converter-filter
---

diff --git a/dlls/quartz/Makefile.in b/dlls/quartz/Makefile.in
--- a/dlls/quartz/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/quartz/Makefile.in
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 SOURCES = \
 	acmwrapper.c \
 	avidec.c \
+	colour.c \
 	control_tlb.idl \
 	decoder.c \
 	dsoundrender.c \

diff --git a/dlls/quartz/colour.c b/dlls/quartz/colour.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/quartz/colour.c
@@ -0,0 +1,462 @@
